## [cb822f0] S platform status apart from the local block; a platform failure does not undo the local block
NOTE S0 Change Log entries written by a plain DecisionService.overturn to BLOCK in this setup :: 2
OK   S1 success: records are PENDING (attempt 1, 0 units) then SUCCEEDED (attempt 1, 20 units); outcome.local and outcome.platform are separate; the verdict is BLOCK with a PENDING BLOCK delivery and only the Change Log entries a plain review writes :: {"local":{"status":"blocked","seq":2,"verdictId":"overturn:channel-a:op-s1"},"records":[{"operationId":"op-s1","eventId":"event-1","channelId":"channel-a","status":"PENDING","reason":null,"attempts":1,"unitsSpent":0},{"operationId":"op-s1","eventId":"event-1","channelId":"channel-a","status":"SUCCEEDED","reason":null,"attempts":1,"unitsSpent":20}],"deliveries":[{"status":"PENDING","downstream":"ALLOW"},{"status":"PENDING","downstream":"BLOCK"}],"changeLogs":[0,2]}
OK   S2 a platform record carries only operationId, eventId, channelId, status, reason, attempts, unitsSpent: no subject key, no message text, no platform message id :: ["attempts","channelId","eventId","operationId","reason","status","unitsSpent"]
OK   S3 the request goes to the event's platform message id, and no database transaction is open while the platform is called :: {"calls":["remove:channel-a:yt-msg-1"],"inTransaction":[false]}
